#!/bin/sh
# Start CortexCode: the released app, exactly as `npx cortexcode` starts it (the installed app in
# ~/.cortexcode/app/, downloaded once when there is none). The app runs the newest frame its updates
# staged and keeps every plugin on the latest release by itself. There is no development build:
# changes reach the app only through releases (scripts/release.sh).
#
# Usage: cortexcode [app options, e.g. --headless or --safe]   (a link to this file works too)
self="$0"
# Follow links (e.g. ~/.local/bin/cortexcode) to this file in the repository.
while [ -L "$self" ]; do
  target="$(readlink "$self")"
  case "$target" in
    /*) self="$target" ;;
    *) self="$(dirname "$self")/$target" ;;
  esac
done
cd "$(dirname "$self")" || exit 1
unset CORTEX_NO_HANDOVER
exec node npm/cortexcode/bin/cortexcode.mjs "$@"
